# Claude Init — BMAD Project

> **Auto-read on every Claude session.** This file reminds Claude (and Chidi) about the golden rule before touching any code.

---

## ⚡ Golden Rule

```
ALWAYS PULL BEFORE YOU START
ALWAYS PUSH WHEN YOU'RE DONE
```

### Why?
Rifat and Chidi are collaborating on the same repo. If you start coding without pulling first, you risk working on stale code and creating merge conflicts.

---

## 🔄 Standard Claude Session Flow

```bash
# 1. Pull latest changes BEFORE doing anything
git pull origin main

# 2. Do your work (edit, create, fix)
# ...

# 3. Commit and push when done
git add -A
git commit -m "your message"
git push origin main
```

---

## 🛑 If You Forget to Pull

If Claude starts work and you haven't pulled:

```bash
git stash          # save your current changes
git pull origin main   # get the latest
git stash pop      # re-apply your changes
```

---

## 📋 Quick Checklist (Run This Every Time)

- [ ] `git pull origin main` — Got the latest?
- [ ] `git status` — Clean working tree?
- [ ] Do the work
- [ ] `git add -A && git commit -m "..."`
- [ ] `git push origin main`
- [ ] Verify: `git log --oneline -3`

---

> *"Pull before you push. The only thing worse than a bug is a merge conflict."* 📎
